  "id": "exponential-distribution",
  "term": "exponential distribution",
  "definition": "The exponential distribution is a statistical distribution often used to describe how long it takes until an event occurs, such as the lifetime of a manufactured item or the time until disease remission. A key feature is its memoryless property, meaning the future waiting time does not depend on how much time has already passed.",
